* smoke test: x1, x2 in [0,3]; constraint x1 + x2 <= 3
*
* Each variable x{i} is a sum of bits: x{i} = 2*x{i}b1 + 1*x{i}b0.
* For each value v we name an order atom x{i}ge{v}, meaning "x{i} >= v",
* and channel it to the bits in both directions:
*   _up:  x{i}ge{v} -> x{i} >= v        bits + v*~ge >= v
*   _dn:  x{i} >= v -> x{i}ge{v}        (U-bits) + (U-v+1)*ge >= U-v+1
* where U = 3 is the largest value the bits can take.
@x1ge1_up 2 x1b1 1 x1b0 1 ~x1ge1 >= 1 ;
@x1ge1_dn 2 ~x1b1 1 ~x1b0 3 x1ge1 >= 3 ;
@x1ge2_up 2 x1b1 1 x1b0 2 ~x1ge2 >= 2 ;
@x1ge2_dn 2 ~x1b1 1 ~x1b0 2 x1ge2 >= 2 ;
@x1ge3_up 2 x1b1 1 x1b0 3 ~x1ge3 >= 3 ;
@x1ge3_dn 2 ~x1b1 1 ~x1b0 1 x1ge3 >= 1 ;
@x2ge1_up 2 x2b1 1 x2b0 1 ~x2ge1 >= 1 ;
@x2ge1_dn 2 ~x2b1 1 ~x2b0 3 x2ge1 >= 3 ;
@x2ge2_up 2 x2b1 1 x2b0 2 ~x2ge2 >= 2 ;
@x2ge2_dn 2 ~x2b1 1 ~x2b0 2 x2ge2 >= 2 ;
@x2ge3_up 2 x2b1 1 x2b0 3 ~x2ge3 >= 3 ;
@x2ge3_dn 2 ~x2b1 1 ~x2b0 1 x2ge3 >= 1 ;
* x1 + x2 <= 3
@lin1 2 x1b1 1 x1b0 2 x2b1 1 x2b0 <= 3 ;
